{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789396508,"nonce":"vdM29cg+ReOK/qwVlskGa7ZouLA=","title":"Fiber.suspend on a krio stack does not suspend","message":"fiber_suspend only set the pending suspend action, which the\ninterpreter loop honours by resuming the caller; on a krio-backed fiber\nthe loop runs on the fiber's own stack with no caller recorded, so the\naction did nothing and the body ran on past the suspend\n(runtime::vm::tests::test_interpret_fiber_suspend under\nWLIFT_KRIO_FIBER=1 printed \"after\"). A suspended fiber hands its\ncaller null and resumes where it stopped if called again, which on a\nkrio stack is exactly a yield of null: fiber_suspend now takes the\nkrio yield path first, as Fiber.yield does.","files":null}]}